{"content_hash": "941604b40c2f358e", "version_id": 685, "article_id": 69, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Father fined €3,000 after toddler's fatal fall from Cyprus hotel window", "title_zh": "父亲因两岁儿子从塞浦路斯酒店窗户坠亡被罚款3000欧元", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj6j1klez88o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1437943085269-6da5dd4295bf?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MTB8fGRhZCUyMGZpbmVkJTIwc29ufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTIxOTQ0ODR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Steven Van Loy on Unsplash", "author": "Steven Van Loy", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@mafalou?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/man-wears-blue-crew-neck-t-shirt-holding-toddler-wears-black-hooded-jacket-near-ocean-under-blue-sky-at-daytime-oUhSla4L_98?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(165, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(203, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "f11dca163925"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-17", "word_count": 268, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "A British father whose two-year-old son fell to his death from a hotel window in Cyprus has been fined €3,000. The court heard that the man mistook the window for being closed when he placed the child on the sill.", "lead_zh": "一名英国父亲因两岁儿子从塞浦路斯酒店窗户坠亡，被法院罚款3000欧元。法庭获悉，这位父亲误以为窗户是关着的，才把孩子放到了窗台上。", "preview": "Joshua Foster, 37, an auditor from Essex, was sentenced by Paphos District Court after admitting to causing his son's death through a reckle", "preview_zh": "37岁的乔舒亚·福斯特来自埃塞克斯，是一名审计师。他承认因鲁莽、轻率或危险的行为导致儿子死亡，帕福斯地区法院因此作出判决。7月12日，这家人在霍拉卡开始度假的第一天，这名幼儿从五星级的国王埃维尔顿海滩度假酒店四楼窗户坠落，高度近40英尺（12.1米）。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 675, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 93.925, "size_bytes": 564480, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 304, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_c1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 96.65, "size_bytes": 580896, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 304, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_c1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_c1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 103.25, "size_bytes": 620496, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 304, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_c1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_c1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 89.25, "size_bytes": 536400, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 304, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_c1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_c1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 95.575, "size_bytes": 574416, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 304, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/69/en_c1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@2388497/content/data/versions/685.json", "paragraphs": ["Joshua Foster, 37, an auditor from Essex, was sentenced by Paphos District Court after admitting to causing his son's death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act. The toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) from a fourth-floor window at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas.", "The court previously heard that Foster had thought the window was closed when he placed his son on the sill to show him a waterpark below, and then \"lost control\" of him. District Judge Froso Christodoulidou noted that the window bore no markings that would necessarily have alerted Foster to the fact that one section was open; his failure to establish that it was not closed led to the tragic outcome.", "In a voluntary statement to police, Foster said the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\". While alcohol was in his system, it did not form a significant part of the case, and his lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, said there was no testimony that he was drunk. The judge stressed there was no evidence Foster had deliberately exposed the child to danger, adding that no sentence could outweigh the personal consequences of losing his child.", "After sentencing, Foster told reporters he looked forward to going home to his wife and daughter. His family said in a statement that they were relieved the process was over, but that the consequences of the tragedy would never end. Alexandrou argued the case should never have gone to court, describing his client as an \"incredible father\" and an exemplary family man."], "paragraphs_zh": ["37岁的乔舒亚·福斯特来自埃塞克斯，是一名审计师。他承认因鲁莽、轻率或危险的行为导致儿子死亡，帕福斯地区法院因此作出判决。7月12日，这家人在霍拉卡开始度假的第一天，这名幼儿从五星级的国王埃维尔顿海滩度假酒店四楼窗户坠落，高度近40英尺（12.1米）。", "法庭此前获悉，福斯特以为窗户是关着的，便把儿子放在窗台上看下面的水上乐园，随后“失手”没抓住他。地区法官弗罗索·赫里斯托祖利杜指出，窗户上没有任何标记必然提醒福斯特其中一扇是开着的；他未能确认窗户并未关闭，最终导致了这一悲剧。", "在自愿向警方提供的陈述中，福斯特说儿子“在他来得及抓住之前就掉了下去”。虽然他体内有酒精，但这并未成为案件的重要部分，他的律师亚历山德罗斯·亚历山德鲁也表示没有证词表明他喝醉了。法官强调，没有证据表明福斯特故意将孩子置于危险之中，并补充说任何判决都无法抵消失去孩子给他个人带来的后果。", "宣判后，福斯特告诉记者，他期待回家与妻子和女儿团聚。他的家人发表声明称，他们对诉讼结束感到宽慰，但这场悲剧的后果永远不会结束。亚历山德鲁认为此案本不该上法庭，并称他的当事人是“一位了不起的父亲”，也是一位模范的家庭男人。"], "body": "Joshua Foster, 37, an auditor from Essex, was sentenced by Paphos District Court after admitting to causing his son's death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act. The toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) from a fourth-floor window at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas.\n\nThe court previously heard that Foster had thought the window was closed when he placed his son on the sill to show him a waterpark below, and then \"lost control\" of him. District Judge Froso Christodoulidou noted that the window bore no markings that would necessarily have alerted Foster to the fact that one section was open; his failure to establish that it was not closed led to the tragic outcome.\n\nIn a voluntary statement to police, Foster said the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\". While alcohol was in his system, it did not form a significant part of the case, and his lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, said there was no testimony that he was drunk. The judge stressed there was no evidence Foster had deliberately exposed the child to danger, adding that no sentence could outweigh the personal consequences of losing his child.\n\nAfter sentencing, Foster told reporters he looked forward to going home to his wife and daughter. His family said in a statement that they were relieved the process was over, but that the consequences of the tragedy would never end. Alexandrou argued the case should never have gone to court, describing his client as an \"incredible father\" and an exemplary family man.", "body_zh": "37岁的乔舒亚·福斯特来自埃塞克斯，是一名审计师。他承认因鲁莽、轻率或危险的行为导致儿子死亡，帕福斯地区法院因此作出判决。7月12日，这家人在霍拉卡开始度假的第一天，这名幼儿从五星级的国王埃维尔顿海滩度假酒店四楼窗户坠落，高度近40英尺（12.1米）。\n\n法庭此前获悉，福斯特以为窗户是关着的，便把儿子放在窗台上看下面的水上乐园，随后“失手”没抓住他。地区法官弗罗索·赫里斯托祖利杜指出，窗户上没有任何标记必然提醒福斯特其中一扇是开着的；他未能确认窗户并未关闭，最终导致了这一悲剧。\n\n在自愿向警方提供的陈述中，福斯特说儿子“在他来得及抓住之前就掉了下去”。虽然他体内有酒精，但这并未成为案件的重要部分，他的律师亚历山德罗斯·亚历山德鲁也表示没有证词表明他喝醉了。法官强调，没有证据表明福斯特故意将孩子置于危险之中，并补充说任何判决都无法抵消失去孩子给他个人带来的后果。\n\n宣判后，福斯特告诉记者，他期待回家与妻子和女儿团聚。他的家人发表声明称，他们对诉讼结束感到宽慰，但这场悲剧的后果永远不会结束。亚历山德鲁认为此案本不该上法庭，并称他的当事人是“一位了不起的父亲”，也是一位模范的家庭男人。", "text": "Joshua Foster, 37, an auditor from Essex, was sentenced by Paphos District Court after admitting to causing his son's death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act. The toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) from a fourth-floor window at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas. The court previously heard that Foster had thought the window was closed when he placed his son on the sill to show him a waterpark below, and then \"lost control\" of him. District Judge Froso Christodoulidou noted that the window bore no markings that would necessarily have alerted Foster to the fact that one section was open; his failure to establish that it was not closed led to the tragic outcome. In a voluntary statement to police, Foster said the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\". While alcohol was in his system, it did not form a significant part of the case, and his lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, said there was no testimony that he was drunk. The judge stressed there was no evidence Foster had deliberately exposed the child to danger, adding that no sentence could outweigh the personal consequences of losing his child. After sentencing, Foster told reporters he looked forward to going home to his wife and daughter. His family said in a statement that they were relieved the process was over, but that the consequences of the tragedy would never end. Alexandrou argued the case should never have gone to court, describing his client as an \"incredible father\" and an exemplary family man.", "vocab": [{"word": "auditor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "审计师", "note": "指从事审计工作的专业人员。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "reckless", "pos": "adj", "zh": "鲁莽的，轻率的", "note": "常与 act、behaviour 等搭配，表示不顾后果。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "sill", "pos": "noun", "zh": "窗台", "note": "window sill 的简称，指窗户底部的横档。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "toddler", "pos": "noun", "zh": "幼儿，学步儿童", "note": "通常指1至3岁刚学会走路的孩子。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fatal", "pos": "adj", "zh": "致命的", "note": "fatal fall/accident 表示导致死亡的坠落或事故。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "custody", "pos": "noun", "zh": "拘留，监护", "note": "in custody 表示被拘留；也可指对孩子的监护权。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "testimony", "pos": "noun", "zh": "证词，证言", "note": "法律语境中指证人在法庭上所说的话。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "voluntary", "pos": "adj", "zh": "自愿的", "note": "voluntary statement 指主动向警方提供的陈述。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "outweigh", "pos": "verb", "zh": "超过，重于", "note": "常表示某事物的重要性或影响大于另一事物。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "exemplary", "pos": "adj", "zh": "模范的，典范的", "note": "形容人时表示堪为榜样的。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "grieve", "pos": "verb", "zh": "悲伤，哀悼", "note": "指因失去亲人等而感到悲痛。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inconceivable", "pos": "adj", "zh": "难以置信的，无法想象的", "note": "表示某事极不可能或难以理解。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pronounced dead", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "被宣告死亡", "note": "常用于医院或事故现场确认死亡。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "relieved", "pos": "adj", "zh": "宽慰的，释然的", "note": "表示因某事结束或好转而感到轻松。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dad fined after son, 2, died in Cyprus hotel fall", "summary_original": "Joshua Foster \"lost control\" of his son while showing him the view of a water park from a window.", "body_original": "Dad fined after son, 2, died in Cyprus hotel fall\nBy\nLewis Adams\nEssex\nPublished\n16 October 2026, 10:31 BST\nUpdated 9 hours ago\nA father whose two-year-old boy fell from a fourth floor window of a Cyprus hotel has been fined €3,000 (£2,500) for causing his death.\nJoshua Foster thought the window was closed when he placed his son on a sill to show him the view of a waterpark\nand \"lost control\" of him\n, Paphos District Court previously heard.\nThe toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas.\nFoster, 37, from Essex, admitted causing death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act and was sentenced earlier.\nHe told reporters afterwards: \"Thank you for the support. I'm looking forward to going home and being with my wife and daughter.\"\nLater, the family said in a statement: \"We are relieved that this process is now over, but for our family, the consequences of this tragedy will never end.\n\"Our son was deeply loved and will be forever missed. His loss is something we carry with us every day.\"\nFoster, an auditor, arrived in Cyprus hours before the incident with his wife, two children and in-laws.\nThey enjoyed various activities and swimming, before getting ready for dinner in the evening.\nAt about 18:00, Foster, his father-in-law and son were walking towards a lift when the boy noticed a waterpark outside.\nFoster pushed the lift button, placed the child on the windowsill and the \"inconceivable\" unfolded before he could react, the court heard.\nThe boy was taken to Paphos General Hospital and later pronounced dead.\n\"The window did not appear to carry markings that would necessarily have alerted the defendant to the fact that one section was open,\" said District Judge Froso Christodoulidou.\nHis failure to establish that the window was not closed led to the tragic result, the judge added.\n\"It was a momentary error which created a dangerous situation with fatal consequences,\" he said.\nThe judge added there was \"no evidence that the defendant deliberately exposed the child to danger\", according to a translation of proceedings.\nShe added no sentence could outweigh the \"personal consequences of the loss of his child\".\nIn a voluntary statement to police, Foster said when he placed his son on the windowsill, the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\".\nWhile Foster had alcohol in his system, it did not form a significant part of the case against him and his lawyer Alexandros Alexandrou said there was no testimony he was drunk.\nAfter the sentencing, Foster's lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, told reporters the case should have \"never gone to court\".\nHe said Foster was held in custody for eight days immediately after the incident and he had to call his daughter from custody to explain what had happened.\n\"Within this three months, there was a lost opportunity for this man to grieve as he wanted to, to be with his family,\" he said.\nHe described his client as an \"incredible father\".\n\"[He is] an exemplary family man with a beautiful family behind him, that support him, that embraces him, that has always been by his side.\"\nDo you have a story suggestion for Essex? Contact us below.\nGet in touch\nYour Voice\nContact form\nContact form\nFollow Essex news on\nBBC Sounds\n,\nFacebook\n,\nexternal\n,\nInstagram\n,\nexternal\nand\nX\n,\nexternal\n.\nRelated topics\nEssex\nPaphos\nCyprus\nMore on this story\nDad sees son fall to death from Cyprus hotel window\nPublished\n6 October\nFather admits causing death of his son in hotel fall\nPublished\n22 September\nRelated internet links\nHM Courts & Tribunals Service", "fetched_at": "2026-10-16T23:48:02.449828", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Joshua", "s": 0.3, "e": 0.725, "sm": 300, "em": 725, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Foster", "s": 0.725, "e": 1.375, "sm": 725, "em": 1375, "cs": 7, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 1.375, "e": 1.488, "sm": 1375, "em": 1487, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "37", "s": 1.488, "e": 2.425, "sm": 1487, "em": 2424, "cs": 15, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": ",", "s": 2.425, "e": 2.525, "sm": 2425, "em": 2525, "cs": 17, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "an", "s": 2.525, "e": 2.663, "sm": 2525, "em": 2662, "cs": 19, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "auditor", "s": 2.663, "e": 3.075, "sm": 2662, "em": 3075, "cs": 22, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "from", "s": 3.075, "e": 3.25, "sm": 3075, "em": 3249, "cs": 30, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "Essex", "s": 3.25, "e": 4.025, "sm": 3250, "em": 4025, "cs": 35, "ce": 40, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": ",", "s": 4.025, "e": 4.125, "sm": 4025, "em": 4124, "cs": 40, "ce": 41, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "was", "s": 4.125, "e": 4.275, "sm": 4125, "em": 4275, "